{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033032-spells-that-are-naturally-lasting","id":1033032,"title":"Spells that are naturally Lasting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-16T17:27:33-08:00","id":1033032,"title":"Spells that are naturally Lasting","content":"Just a little something that has me curious. Mostly for spells that don't outright say that their duration is lasting, but can be assumed that they are from the description and effects they have. I was recently in an argument with my ST that the Shaping rote for Matter would only temporarily bend an object into a shape. Once you were done it would go right back to its previous shape. For example, I could Shape a block of wood into a sculpture and it would then shunt itself back into place.<br /> <br /> I'd like the Forum's opinion on this and possibly even your own thoughts on spells that would otherwise be naturally lasting. Since it seems that most people are against letting it happen unless it specifically says so in the spell itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12814-epicjester","name":"Epicjester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T17:38:42-08:00","id":1033040,"title":"","content":"Things like damage and healing I know by default are lasting. (Lasting side bar mage 113)<br /> <br /> I know that transmutation of one substance to another is not lasting. In this same regard I could see the lie re-asserting itself once the spells duration is up.<br /> <br /> For your specific instance this spell\u2019s reach effect to reduce the number of successes to create or repair an item may be more in line with what you desire. This way you use the magic to help create the object but the objects does not rely on magic to maintain its shape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T17:41:59-08:00","id":1033042,"title":"","content":"From how I understand it you're assuming that the side effect of the spell is the spell itself. Shaping doesn't permanently alter a shape, it temporarily grants you the ability to alter a shape which remains after the spell is gone.<br /> <br /> Other spells, such as Transmutation or Create Ghost are essentially using magic to maintain an otherwise impossible state of reality and when the magic is gone it collapses in on itself and reverts back to the original material or there being no ghost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T17:49:31-08:00","id":1033053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033032-spells-that-are-naturally-lasting?p=1033042#post1033042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From how I understand it you're assuming that the side effect of the spell is the spell itself. Shaping doesn't permanently alter a shape, it temporarily grants you the ability to alter a shape which remains after the spell is gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where the ST and I disagree. He thinks that because I used shaping to craft an item, (Rearranging ink on paper to make a new design) the item would go back to its previous state when the duration is up.I'm of the mind that it sticks. Because otherwise my Moros Alchemist is unable to craft things at all with magic if the pieces just plop back into place when the spell runs out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12814-epicjester","name":"Epicjester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T17:58:20-08:00","id":1033061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epicjester</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033032-spells-that-are-naturally-lasting?p=1033053#post1033053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is where the ST and I disagree. He thinks that because I used shaping to craft an item, (Rearranging ink on paper to make a new design) the item would go back to its previous state when the duration is up.I'm of the mind that it sticks. Because otherwise my Moros Alchemist is unable to craft things at all with magic if the pieces just plop back into place when the spell runs out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you using the reach option to do this crafting? If not I may suggest looking at it. Since in this case it makes something easier to be done I'd personally say the effects are lasting in the same manor that other spells could help you jump higher. If you used a spell to 'empower' yourself to climb a building you wouldn't suddenly find yourself at the bottom. In this same regard by the contract not relying on magic to be maintained, only to be easier to shape in a mundane manor I think it'd be lasting as long as you use that reach effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T18:29:24-08:00","id":1033076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epicjester</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033032-spells-that-are-naturally-lasting?p=1033053#post1033053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is where the ST and I disagree. He thinks that because I used shaping to craft an item, (Rearranging ink on paper to make a new design) the item would go back to its previous state when the duration is up.I'm of the mind that it sticks. Because otherwise my Moros Alchemist is unable to craft things at all with magic if the pieces just plop back into place when the spell runs out.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could bring up other examples and ask how that works. For instance, a Knowing Matter spell allows you to discern the composition of a material, does that mean the information of what the material is made of leaves your head when the spell ends? Obviously the answer is no or there wouldn't be any point to casting a Knowing spell. Gaining information also has a physical effect on your brain by the way, and if he's allowed you to keep info from a Knowing spell then he's now also allowed permanent physical side effects from using magic. If he still disagrees I'd point out that this means you can kill everyone with magic and when your spell's Duration ends they'll just come back to life and that this means you're also immune to being killed with spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T00:16:11-08:00","id":1033197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epicjester</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033032-spells-that-are-naturally-lasting?p=1033053#post1033053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is where the ST and I disagree. He thinks that because I used shaping to craft an item, (Rearranging ink on paper to make a new design) the item would go back to its previous state when the duration is up.I'm of the mind that it sticks. Because otherwise my Moros Alchemist is unable to craft things at all with magic if the pieces just plop back into place when the spell runs out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your ST is correct, I was having the same discussion about 'transmutation' spells as Legacy Attainments for the Uncrowned Kings in early days after 2E premiere. BUT at Matter 2 you got Arcanum Attainment:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtAw 2E, p 193</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Matter 2: Permanence</b><br /> Changing an object\u2019s nature and properties is easier than changing the nature of a living being. An Apprentice of Matter need simply make a small investment of energy to an object to make any Matter spell\u2019s effects long-lasting.<br /> System: The character may spend one Mana instead of using a Reach to use the Advanced Duration spell factor of a spell with Matter as its highest Arcanum</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-17-2017, 03:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T00:20:13-08:00","id":1033199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033032-spells-that-are-naturally-lasting?p=1033197#post1033197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your ST is correct</div> </div> </div> </div>The spell has Potency as its Primary Factor and specifically mentions using it for things that a snapback would render nonsensical in the second Reach effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T01:18:00-08:00","id":1033221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033032-spells-that-are-naturally-lasting?p=1033197#post1033197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your ST is correct, I was having the same discussion about 'transmutation' spells as Legacy Attainments for the Uncrowned Kings in early days after 2E premiere. BUT at Matter 2 you got Arcanum Attainment:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that a shape is not part of a thing's nature or property.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T02:06:01-08:00","id":1033241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033032-spells-that-are-naturally-lasting?p=1033199#post1033199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spell has Potency as its Primary Factor and specifically mentions using it for things that a snapback would render nonsensical in the second Reach effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Your storyteller is wrong Epicjester. Rule of thumb is, that if the change is caused through the spells effect, but not by the spell itself, it is lasting. This by the way shows why Transubstantiation is the exactly opposite of Shaping for considering lasting effects.<br /> With Transubstantiation the spell effect is, that one material is changed into a different one. If the spell ends, this effect ends, so the material changes back to what it was. If you change a block of steel into putty, make a sculpture out of the putty and then let the spell end, you got a sculpture out of steel. The form doesn't change back, because it was not changed by the spell itself, but by mundane means.<br /> Same goes for Shaping. The effect of the spell is to make matter &quot;shapeable&quot; even in defiance of gravity. If you use it to shape a block of steel into a sculpture again and the spell ends, you can no longer shape the material, because the effect of the spell is gone, but the current form sticks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","user":"HardcoreHannes","date":". 01-17-2017, 05:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T02:48:49-08:00","id":1033247,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you were just moving the ink. That's not going to revert.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T06:50:36-08:00","id":1033324,"title":"","content":"I am in the &quot;Commanding objects with your mind is the spell, the results are not a part of it&quot; camp, for many reasons but none so much as the idea of a particularly frustrating player deciding to try and weaponize this; shaping ink onto parchment, placing the ink bottle somewhere else, and watching as the spell comes undone and the ink proceeds to fly at supersonic speeds back to the ink well and shatters everything in its way.<br /> <br /> You might think it's silly but sometimes you just get that one guy who is willing to calculate the energetic release of a mass of India ink sufficient to quill a page traveling a certain distance in a three second span.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T08:13:25-08:00","id":1033373,"title":"","content":"Well thanks to everyone who gave your opinion. The reasoning behind it was sound. Pretty much a lot of you managed to put my own thoughts on the matter (ha) into words. Something magical happens thanks to a spell. But what remains afterwards isn't held in place by that magic so it would naturally be lasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12814-epicjester","name":"Epicjester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}